diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 26c02b5..00052f6 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -318,6 +318,11 @@ The game can record a gameplay session into a `.dmo` demo file and replay it det
 - `-play [<path>]` / `-play=[<path>]` — play back the first matching `pvzp-*.dmo` recording in descending timestamp/name order, or an explicit `<path>` if given.
 - `-playnum <N>` / `-playnum=<N>` — play back the N-th recording in descending timestamp/name order; `1` selects the first.
 - `-recnum <N>` / `-recnum=<N>` — record and keep the first `N` files matching the automatic timestamp pattern in descending timestamp/name order; other `pvzp-*.dmo` files are left untouched.
+- `-play-to-end` — fast-forward demo playback to completion for deterministic regression verification; the replay window uses a distinct title so a tiling window manager can place it independently.
+- `-play-to <update>` / `-play-to=<update>` — fast-forward through the requested update, write the verification report if configured, and exit; useful for checking a marked trajectory prefix without replaying an idle tail.
+- `-demo-blackout` — skip intermediate presentation while fast-forwarding; after the minimal title-screen draws required to start resource loading, the window remains black while the Metal-backed simulation runs.
+- `-demo-hidden` — keep the replay window out of the desktop layout; intended for automated verification, and composable with `-demo-blackout`.
+- `-demo-report <path>` / `-demo-report=<path>` — write a machine-readable completion, length-mismatch, or divergence report for demo verification.
 
 This feature is primarily designed for debugging and regression testing.
 
